# Normalize line endings for everything Git detects as text: store as LF in
# the repo and check out as LF too (eol=lf overrides each machine's local
# core.autocrlf). Without this, syncing the working tree between machines
# with different autocrlf settings (e.g. via Syncthing) makes Git think
# every text file changed on the next `git status`, even when the content
# is byte-identical — that's what was happening before this file existed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binary types — never run line-ending/diff text handling on these.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
